  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "You are given an array AAA of NNN integers.\n\nYou can perform the following operation as many times as you want (possibly 000):\n\n\nChoose index iii (1≤i≤N1 \\le i \\le N1≤i≤N), and multiply AiA_iAi​ by 222.\nFind the **minimum** possible value of max⁡(A)−min⁡(A)\\max(A) - \\min(A)max(A)−min(A) you can achieve through the use of the operations.\n\n\nInput Format\n\nThe first line of input will contain a single integer TTT, denoting the number of test cases.\nEach test case consists of multiple lines of input.\n\nThe first line contains NNN - the size of the array.\nThe second line contains NNN integers - A1,A2,…,ANA_1, A_2, \\ldots, A_NA1​,A2​,…,AN​.\n\n\n\n\nOutput Format\nFor each test case, output on a new line the minimum possible value of max⁡(A)−min⁡(A)\\max(A) - \\min(A)max(A)−min(A) possible with the use of several operations.",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤T≤1041 \\le T \\le 10^41≤T≤104",
      "2≤N≤1052 \\le N \\le 10^52≤N≤105",
      "1≤Ai≤1051 \\le A_i \\le 10^51≤Ai​≤105",
      "The sum of NNN over all test cases does not exceed 10510^5105."
    ],
    "inputFormat": "",
    "outputFormat": "",
    "notes": [],
